  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 147 PM CDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nHot and dry conditions will continue for another day before the\nrain chances creep into the forecast, mainly across the eastern\nhalf. Although a heat advisory currently isn't issued, tomorrow\nshould still be a warm day, however, heat index values are \nexpected to remain below criteria. Remember that cumulative heat \nstress can result in a higher risk of heat illness. Please use \ncaution if you are spending time outside. Drink plenty of water \nand take breaks. Don't forget to look before you lock! Low end \nrain chances (15-30%) will enter the forecast Thursday night with \nthe best chances for rain being Saturday (30-60%) across the \nVictoria Crossroads. Dry conditions should return by Sunday.\n\nMore heat safety information can be found at weather.gov/heat",
